{
  "esm": "0.8.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "GEOSFP_A1_loader",
    "description": "Pure-I/O data loader for GEOS-FP (A1 collection): 1-hourly time-averaged single-level (2-D surface) diagnostics on the native 0.3125°×0.25° global longitude/latitude grid, from the GEOS-Chem GEOS_FP 0.25x0.3125 archive.\n\nThis is one loader half of the geosfp loader+regridding-model split (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §4.1/§7; bead esm-3nc.2, following the esm-3nc.1 era5/wrf pattern). It is PURE I/O: it declares its source (url_template), the file variables it reads (with units), its temporal cadence, and its NATIVE grid expressed as a GDD Grid with a geographic (longlat/WGS84) crs descriptor. It performs NO reprojection and NO regridding — those are per-variable concerns of the regridding model (components/earthsci_data/geosfp.esm), which references this file as a subsystem via {\"ref\": \"./geosfp_a1_loader.esm\"} under the subsystem key GEOSFP_A1.\n\nThe removed co-located blocks: the old DataLoaderSpatial block (proj4 crs string / grid_type / staggering / resolution / extent) is replaced by the GDD `grid` (family + crs + dimensions + extents); the old per-loader `regridding` block (fill_value / extrapolation) is gone — regridding is declared per-variable on the model (geosfp.esm `regrid`). Because a `temporal` block is present, this loader seeds DISCRETE cadence (ess-v9a.5): the runtime refreshes the file buffers on its update schedule.\n\nMigrated from EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/geosfp.jl (GEOSFPFileSet, filetype=A1). Split out of the pre-migration components/earthsci_data/geosfp.esm (esm-1c6s).",
    "tags": [
      "earthsci_data",
      "meteorology",
      "geos_fp",
      "global",
      "data_loader",
      "pure-io",
      "longlat"
    ],
    "created": "2026-06-25T00:00:00Z",
    "authors": [
      "NASA GMAO / GEOS-Chem",
      "EarthSciModels migration (esm-3nc.2)"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "GEOS-FP data archived for GEOS-Chem classic. NASA Global Modeling and Assimilation Office (GMAO). AWS S3 mirror: s3://geos-chem/GEOS_{domain}/GEOS_FP/. See http://geoschemdata.wustl.edu/ExtData/ for current domain and file-type options.",
        "url": "http://geoschemdata.wustl.edu/ExtData/"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Molod, A., Takacs, L., Suarez, M., and Bacmeister, J. (2015). Development of the GEOS-5 atmospheric general circulation model: evolution from MERRA to MERRA2. Geosci. Model Dev., 8, 1339–1356.",
        "doi": "10.5194/gmd-8-1339-2015"
      },
      {
        "citation": "GEOS-Chem vertical grid documentation: https://wiki.seas.harvard.edu/geos-chem/index.php/GEOS-Chem_vertical_grids",
        "url": "https://wiki.seas.harvard.edu/geos-chem/index.php/GEOS-Chem_vertical_grids"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Source: EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/geosfp.jl (GEOSFPFileSet, GEOSFP constructor, Ap/Bp hybrid grid coefficients, geosfp_staggering). Test: test/geosfp_test.jl. Docs: docs present in pinned commit."
      }
    ]
  },
  "data_loaders": {
    "GEOSFP_A1": {
      "kind": "grid",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "https://geos-chem.s3-us-west-2.amazonaws.com/GEOS_0.25x0.3125/GEOS_FP/{date:%Y}/{date:%m}/GEOSFP.{date:%Y%m%d}.A1.025x03125.nc"
      },
      "temporal": {
        "start": "2013-01-01T00:30:00Z",
        "file_period": "P1D",
        "frequency": "PT1H",
        "records_per_file": 24,
        "time_variable": "time"
      },
      "variables": {
        "T2M": {
          "file_variable": "T2M",
          "units": "K",
          "description": "Air temperature at 2m above displacement height. Time-averaged over 1-hour interval centered at record time."
        },
        "QV2M": {
          "file_variable": "QV2M",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "description": "Specific humidity at 2m above displacement height. Time-averaged over 1-hour interval."
        },
        "U10M": {
          "file_variable": "U10M",
          "units": "m/s",
          "description": "Eastward (zonal) wind at 10m above displacement height. Time-averaged over 1-hour interval."
        },
        "V10M": {
          "file_variable": "V10M",
          "units": "m/s",
          "description": "Northward (meridional) wind at 10m above displacement height. Time-averaged over 1-hour interval."
        },
        "PBLH": {
          "file_variable": "PBLH",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "Planetary boundary layer height (m). Time-averaged over 1-hour interval."
        },
        "PRECTOT": {
          "file_variable": "PRECTOT",
          "units": "kg/m^2/s",
          "description": "Total precipitation rate (large-scale + convective). Time-averaged over 1-hour interval."
        },
        "PRECANV": {
          "file_variable": "PRECANV",
          "units": "kg/m^2/s",
          "description": "Anvil precipitation rate. Time-averaged over 1-hour interval."
        },
        "SLP": {
          "file_variable": "SLP",
          "units": "Pa",
          "description": "Sea-level pressure. Time-averaged over 1-hour interval."
        },
        "TS": {
          "file_variable": "TS",
          "units": "K",
          "description": "Surface skin temperature. Time-averaged over 1-hour interval."
        },
        "CLDTOT": {
          "file_variable": "CLDTOT",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Total cloud fraction (0–1). Time-averaged over 1-hour interval."
        },
        "SWGDN": {
          "file_variable": "SWGDN",
          "units": "W/m^2",
          "description": "Incident shortwave flux at ground (W m⁻²). Time-averaged over 1-hour interval."
        },
        "TROPP_H": {
          "file_variable": "TROPP_H",
          "units": "Pa",
          "description": "Tropopause pressure using the thermal definition (Pa). Time-averaged over 1-hour interval."
        },
        "EFLUX": {
          "file_variable": "EFLUX",
          "units": "W/m^2",
          "description": "Latent heat flux from turbulence (W/m^2), positive upward. Time-averaged over 1-hour interval. The moisture counterpart to HFLUX: a boundary-layer scheme needs BOTH to form the VIRTUAL heat flux w'theta_v' = w'theta'*(1+0.61*QV2M) + 0.61*T2M*w'q', which is what sets buoyancy and hence the Monin-Obukhov length and the convective velocity scale. HFLUX alone drops the moisture term and systematically under-predicts instability over moist surfaces."
        },
        "FRSEAICE": {
          "file_variable": "FRSEAICE",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Sea ice area fraction (0–1). Time-averaged over 1-hour interval."
        },
        "GWETTOP": {
          "file_variable": "GWETTOP",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Topsoil wetness (dimensionless). Time-averaged over 1-hour interval."
        },
        "LAI": {
          "file_variable": "LAI",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Leaf area index (m² m⁻²). Time-averaged over 1-hour interval."
        },
        "USTAR": {
          "file_variable": "USTAR",
          "units": "m/s",
          "description": "Surface friction velocity (m/s). Time-averaged over 1-hour interval."
        },
        "HFLUX": {
          "file_variable": "HFLUX",
          "units": "W/m^2",
          "description": "Sensible heat flux from turbulence (W/m^2), positive upward. Time-averaged over 1-hour interval. Needed together with TS and USTAR to form the Monin-Obukhov length L = -rho_air*Cp*Ts*u_star^3/(vK*g*HFLUX), the stability input to Wesley (1989) dry deposition — see AtmosphericDeposition.jl ext/EarthSciDataExt.jl couple2(DryDepositionGasCoupler, GEOSFPCoupler)."
        },
        "Z0M": {
          "file_variable": "Z0M",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "Surface roughness length for momentum (m). Time-averaged over 1-hour interval."
        }
      },
      "reference": {
        "citation": "GEOS-FP A1 collection. NASA GMAO. AWS mirror: geos-chem.s3-us-west-2.amazonaws.com/GEOS_0.25x0.3125/GEOS_FP/",
        "url": "http://geoschemdata.wustl.edu/ExtData/"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "geos_fp",
          "meteorology",
          "surface",
          "1-hourly",
          "2d"
        ],
        "earthscidata_source": "src/geosfp.jl::GEOSFPFileSet (filetype=A1)",
        "filetype": "A1",
        "domain": "0.25x0.3125",
        "time_center_note": "A1 record times are centered: 00:30, 01:30, ..., 23:30 UTC (Delta_Time=010000). The start field records the center time of the first record on the first day of the archive.",
        "native_resolution_deg": {
          "longitude": 0.3125,
          "latitude": 0.25
        },
        "native_extent": {
          "longitude": [
            -180.0,
            180.0
          ],
          "latitude": [
            -90.0,
            90.0
          ]
        },
        "regridding_provenance": "Former co-located data_loaders.regridding block (fill_value=0.0, extrapolation=clamp) removed in the 0.6.0 hard break; regridding is now declared per-variable on the GEOSFP model `regrid` (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §4.1/§5.2).",
        "crs_provenance": "Former DataLoaderSpatial.crs '+proj=longlat +datum=WGS84 +no_defs' is now the structured GDD grid.crs {projection: longlat, datum: WGS84}."
      }
    }
  }
}
